# Pairs with RestoreConverges, under the fairness Spec asserts. A refusal that
# acknowledges the delivery advances the sender past it, so a post-cutover write
# admitted under a stale cached epoch, or while the copy was closed, is never
# re-shipped and the clusters never converge. The refusal must defer.
MODULE: RestoreConvergesRefusalAcked
TARGET: RestoreConverges
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a refused delivery is acknowledged instead of deferred
PERTURBS: Land
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
         THEN UNCHANGED <<data, sent>>
--- REPLACE
         \* MUTATION: the refusal acks.
         THEN /\ sent' = [sent EXCEPT ![r.from] = @ \cup {r.w}]
              /\ UNCHANGED data
--- END
